  "observations": [
    "Guest collaborator internal repository access differs from ordinary managed users; IdP-provisioned guest role is EMU-only.",
    "Authentication and provisioning must be separately configured; mixed Okta/Entra SSO+SCIM combinations explicitly unsupported in either order.",
    "Enterprise recovery codes differ from personal account codes; SAML recovery codes single-use/consecutive and grant24hours in containing scope.",
    "SAML credential authorization revocation is not deletion of underlying token/key; disabling SAML retains credentials and authorizations while removing linked identities.",
    "Conflict resolution varies by needs-access, SCIM organization provisioning and enterprise SAML; no universal destructive operation.",
    "GHES JIT offboarding requires manual account suspension; IdP removal alone leaves token/SSH authentication possible.",
    "Public repository access exemptions distinguish overview/files/fork/Git reads from issues/PR/projects/releases.",
    "SAML external identity GraphQL access differs between orgowner/token/Appinstall scope and enterpriseownertoken; enterprise App access not supported.",
    "Session refresh thresholds2hours/5minutes and recommended4hours retained; clock-skew guidance differs byplatform and ADFS.",
    "SCIM membership changes should originate from IdP; manual invite/removal can leave unlinked/stale identities.",
    "Dedicated SCIM configuration account is a recommendation, with orgowner/license prerequisites, not authorized creation.",
    "SCIM org versus EMU enterprise implementations and NameID/userName exact match must remain distinct.",
    "SCIM rate-limit scope1000users/hour perintegration/group oncloud versus optional siteconfiguredserver limits; IdP recovery behavior varies.",
    "PUT/PATCH audit events preserve conditionals; an event name list is not actual runtime receipt.",
    "Trial link and historical preview expressions do not grant current feature availability.",
    "Screenshot alttext is not binary image inspection."
  ],
